":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T10:54:25-07:00","id":1406994,"title":"","content":"If I may ask, what had you decide to make a supplement for the Mekhet? Are they simply your favorite clan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T11:07:23-07:00","id":1406995,"title":"","content":"So what's the layout of this book? The original was like novella, with other works of fiction interspersed, which all tied into a story between the four other clan books, and appendices at the end that explained the mechanics of its new splats. So far, this book sounds like the appendices, but more of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T11:17:34-07:00","id":1406998,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24173\" data-vbnamecard=\"24173\">Primordial newcomer</a> from what it seems, they plan on making a 2e Clan Book for every major clan. At least, a Nosferatu teaser of &quot;coming soon&quot; is presented at the end of the book<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3523\" data-vbnamecard=\"3523\">Spencer from The Hills</a> it is less of a novella and more of an supplement, not really an &quot;expanded appendix&quot; as much as its own splat book about providing different options for a Mekhet character<br /> <br /> Personally, I really like what I've seen. While when hearing &quot;Night Horrors&quot; I've thought we'll see something in the style of the Wicked Dead while it is instead two ghoul families and a very unexpected antagonist, it is still all really cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T11:28:42-07:00","id":1407001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1406656-strange-shades-mekhet-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1406998#post1406998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> from what it seems, they plan on making a 2e Clan Book for every major clan. At least, a Nosferatu teaser of &amp;quot;coming soon&amp;quot; is presented at the end of the book<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> it is less of a novella and more of an supplement, not really an &amp;quot;expanded appendix&amp;quot; as much as its own splat book about providing different options for a Mekhet character<br /> <br /> Personally, I really like what I've seen. While when hearing &amp;quot;Night Horrors&amp;quot; I've thought we'll see something in the style of the Wicked Dead while it is instead two ghoul families and a very unexpected antagonist, it is still all really cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh ok, I'm sorry but by they do you mean &quot;they&quot;? Is Yossarian working with others on these books, or do you simply mean Yossarian when you say they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T12:20:46-07:00","id":1407010,"title":"","content":"Like, according to the STV, the book has a number of authors","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T12:22:04-07:00","id":1407011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1406656-strange-shades-mekhet-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1406932#post1406932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while going through the book (which seems to be full of good stuff), I've noticed that in the Prince's Wrath rituals, the ritual self inflict a certain amount of damage to the user equal to 5 - Blood Potency. Assuming this is a error (as BP goes up to 10), should it be 10 - Blood Potency, or 5 - Lithopedia?<br /> <br /> Also, just out of curiosity- is there a reason that you avoided trating Setite Cruac as the Chaos Magic style from Secret of the Covenents other than not wanting to relay on another book?<br /> <br /> Other than that, this update looks really interesting and useful for both players and STs. I'll post a detailed review once Drivethru would let me do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 5 - Blood Potency thing is intentional. If you're 5 or higher, I believe it says you still have to take a minimum of one lethal (though maybe I'll tweak that for final version). Making it 10 - minus BP torps most characters, and I wanted it to be something they could still do at low BP, even if it did carry a fair amount of risk. The narrative reason being that, in Immortal Sinners, Prince's Wrath was a Devotion only high Blood Potency characters could take.<br /> <br /> I did consider adding the Chaos style as one of their Initiation Benefits, but as you said, I didn't want to reference too many other supplements that weren't the core (we kind of did too many as it is), and it didn't really work for human Sethites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T12:26:02-07:00","id":1407013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1406656-strange-shades-mekhet-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1406995#post1406995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the layout of this book? The original was like novella, with other works of fiction interspersed, which all tied into a story between the four other clan books, and appendices at the end that explained the mechanics of its new splats. So far, this book sounds like the appendices, but more of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah, this is a more straightforward mechanical supplement than the original clan books. Partially because we love those books so much, and didn't want to impose upon or continue that story, and partially because those kinds of narrative/artifact books take a lot of planning and resources.<br /> <br /> That said, there is a short story that runs through Strange Shades, and it <i>will </i>connect with any future potential clan book updates/sequels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T12:48:13-07:00","id":1407016,"title":"","content":"Oh wow, 110 pages! Congrats on such a meaty book! I can't wait to dig into this later today, especially the shadow cults. A friend of mine might find those useful for an upcoming Mekhet character.<br /> <br /> This also reminds me I should actually get around to posting more of my bloodline conversions here, like I said I would...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T13:00:48-07:00","id":1407019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1406656-strange-shades-mekhet-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1407016#post1407016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow, 110 pages! Congrats on such a meaty book! I can't wait to dig into this later today, especially the shadow cults. A friend of mine might find those useful for an upcoming Mekhet character.<br /> <br /> This also reminds me I should actually get around to posting more of my bloodline conversions here, like I said I would...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! That 100 page number was actually really important to us. We wanted to make sure people got as much bang for their buck as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T14:00:04-07:00","id":1407026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1406656-strange-shades-mekhet-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1407010#post1407010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, according to the STV, the book has a number of authors</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh, I'm sorry for asking then lol. I'll pay better attention from now on (I hate it when I ask questions like that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T16:57:33-07:00","id":1407048,"title":"","content":"This book is legitimately really good. I guess I was really just expecting a straightforward translation of the 1ed clanbook's appendix. <br /> <br /> I've read/skimmed most of the book now, but everything is really well done, from the formatting, to art, to writing, and there are a lot of really creative ideas and hooks. I'm like straight up impressed with this. Good job Yossarian and team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 08-08-2020, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T18:25:21-07:00","id":1407059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1406656-strange-shades-mekhet-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1407048#post1407048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This book is legitimately really good. I guess I was really just expecting a straightforward translation of the 1ed clanbook's appendix.<br /> <br /> I've skimmed some stuff, but everything is really well done, from the formatting, to art, to writing, and there are a lot of really creative ideas and hooks. I'm like straight up impressed with this. Good job Yossarian and team.</div> </div> </div> </div>We really appreciate it! And if you have a minute, consider leaving us a review. It's a little thing that helps a lot.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I really try to make these STV books as high quality as I can. Almost all the art is commissioned, and we even made sure all the new bloodlines got logos (and the Csalad, who never had one before).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T11:50:10-07:00","id":1407165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1406656-strange-shades-mekhet-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1407019#post1407019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you! That 100 page number was actually really important to us. We wanted to make sure people got as much bang for their buck as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was well earned, I think! There is a lot of really great stuff in here, especially in the Chapter Three. I'm a big fan of the simplified Ka rules and the new numen. I don't like a lot of bookkeeping, and tend to only track Manifestation Conditions when a player's cool stuff needs me to. If I need a ghost to manifest for the story, I can just, like, assume the Open Condition is there, without having to actually keep track of it, y'know? So, rules that make it even easier to do that are great, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> However, what sticks out in my mind the most is the Leandros, and for probably the stupidest reason. They are very similar to a 2e update I did of the Players for some friends, just less of an unapologetically meta shitpost [and probably better for it]. You can imagine how tickled I was when their write-up even name-dropped the Players in the rumors section! I guess it is just a logical direction to take Mekhet with Majesty, but it is a delightful coincidence nonetheless!<br /> <br /> Once again, congrats on the 100+ pages; everyone crammed a lot of fun stuff into them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T13:16:11-07:00","id":1407174,"title":"","content":"So I've finished the book. My biggest criticism is that the Cult rules weren't entirely included. We're y'all unable to include them due to wc restrictions, or because it made use of a kind of proprietary system? <br /> <br /> I generally don't mind, but given that Geist is a completely different line, it's kind of a pain to need to buy an entirely separate core book in order to understand this book's systems.<br /> <br /> I also kind of wish you guys had included a fully statted cult just to kind of model what you guys were getting at. <br /> <br /> Also, maybe I just skimmed this section (I did) but I wasn't too clear on how the Inconnu differ from the Invictus, what their night to night is like, what they use all the humans to do, how exactly they worship the Masquerade, or how they differ from a minor covenant in general. <br /> <br /> My opinion that the book is really good is unchanged. But that is where (I feel like) it could be improved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 08-09-2020, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T13:30:28-07:00","id":1407175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1406656-strange-shades-mekhet-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1407165#post1407165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was well earned, I think! There is a lot of really great stuff in here, especially in the Chapter Three. I'm a big fan of the simplified Ka rules and the new numen. I don't like a lot of bookkeeping, and tend to only track Manifestation Conditions when a player's cool stuff needs me to. If I need a ghost to manifest for the story, I can just, like, assume the Open Condition is there, without having to actually keep track of it, y'know? So, rules that make it even easier to do that are great, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> However, what sticks out in my mind the most is the Leandros, and for probably the stupidest reason. They are very similar to a 2e update I did of the Players for some friends, just less of an unapologetically meta shitpost [and probably better for it]. You can imagine how tickled I was when their write-up even name-dropped the Players in the rumors section! I guess it is just a logical direction to take Mekhet with Majesty, but it is a delightful coincidence nonetheless!<br /> <br /> Once again, congrats on the 100+ pages; everyone crammed a lot of fun stuff into them!</div> </div> </div> </div>I had pretty much the same reaction about the Leandros when I read the first draft, funny enough, and the rumor about them was there from the start. The Leandros are sort of meant as the Players, but not as pathetic. Or, pathetic in a more sinister way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T13:48:56-07:00","id":1407178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1406656-strange-shades-mekhet-now-available-at-storytellers-vault?p=1407174#post1407174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've finished the book. My biggest criticism is that the Cult rules weren't entirely included. We're y'all unable to include them due to wc restrictions, or because it made use of a kind of proprietary system?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Long story short, transferring the full Krewe System over from <b>Geist </b>would have meant an immense amount of copying and pasting without alteration, and I just wasn't comfortable with that, or, I would think, <i>allowed </i>to do that. I also wasn't inclined to try to rewrite the whole thing when the <b>Geist </b>book already says it just fine (the Krewe system is just really good). If this were an official book, I definitely would've included a complete system, but that's the limit of things like STV. But, I also really wanted to include something like the organization system for cults, so this was the awkward compromise. This is why it's only about three pages; I didn't want it to take up a huge amount of space for something you need the <b>Geist </b>core to run.<br /> <br /> As for the Inconnu, I'm not <i>entirely </i>satisfied with the way the final version comes off, so I have a little errata to clarify things/adjust when I update the file for the final version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19